  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper evaluates a Variational Quantum Classifier (VQC) for credit card fraud detection using different feature-selection strategies on a balanced subset of 50,000 transactions from the European Cardholder dataset. The best configuration (PSO + VQC) achieves 94.54% accuracy, outperforming other VQC variants such as ACO (89.70%), ASO (89.12%), and K-Best (84.48%). All experiments are performed on a classical simulator using PennyLane.",
